# 8. COMPARE THREE POSSIBLE ARCHITECTURES

Evaluate at least these alternatives.

## Architecture A — Puck-led editor

- Puck handles component composition, nested sections, and content schema.
- Moveable handles geometric manipulation where supported.
- dnd-kit is introduced only for structural interactions not adequately supported by Puck.
- CSS Grid or React Grid Layout handles suitable collection layouts.
- Motion remains the animation engine.

## Architecture B — Custom visual editor

- A custom component registry and page schema.
- Moveable for geometry.
- dnd-kit for structural drag-and-drop.
- Custom inspector and layers navigator.
- CSS Grid and specialized collection layout engines.
- Motion for animation.

## Architecture C — Hybrid selective integration

- Reuse selected editor framework capabilities.
- Custom interaction overlays.
- Custom protected storefront components.
- Specialized grid manipulation.
- Shared public/editor renderer.
- Minimal editor-only dependencies.

For each architecture, evaluate:

- Compatibility with existing code.
- Risk of changing the landing-page appearance.
- Support for precise resizing and shape editing.
- Nested component support.
- Product/category grid flexibility.
- Mini-preview integration.
- Runtime performance.
- Editor bundle size.
- Production bundle isolation.
- Maintainability.
- Learning curve.
- Future extensibility.
- Licensing.
- Security.
- Development complexity.

Do not select an architecture based on popularity alone.

